# Slice 295 probe (the book :441): the body's root declares `y`, an inline `if` declares `y` again.  The data map is built by
# the root heads: the nested declaration writes the same prepared place, it is no second field (no shadowing).  Entry 7; a
# wrong value leaves as the exit code (v, then 100 + v).
fn: m () int
    int: y 1
    if: y = 1
        int: y 2
    ---
    return: y
end: m
int: code 7
int: v m()
if: v != 2
    code: v
---
if: code = 7 && m\var\y != 2
    code: 100 + m\var\y
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
